// T3-024 (REQ-PERF-003, REQ-TEST-003): the 20,000-soldier fight. Two armies
// of 10,000 each on the 1600 x 1200 m plains: 50 regiments of 200 in 10
// columns of 5 (hastati, hoplites, velites, archers, cavalry cycling by row
// and column, each row's cavalry on the east end) plus a 20-man bodyguard
// and the general, pre-placed with the front rows 200 m apart. Side 0
// (player 0) attack-moves everything at the enemy at tick 20, as perf_10k
// and the `ai_vs_charge` band do; side 1 is the engine AI (player 255).
// Two engine armies were the task's first shape and never met on this map:
// each plan strikes the enemy edge away from the enemy cavalry, and with
// the cavalry on opposite wings the two lines slid to opposite ends of the
// field; with both cavalry wings on the same end the lines converged but
// never dressed, the plan's 300 m line leaving 16 regiments of 200 no room
// to stand in their own formations (docs/09 T3-024, SAD §12 T-15).
// `il_cli bench --scenario` times the whole battle to its end; T3-026 puts
// the file in the determinism corpus with the budget below.
//
